# TechAgenz – Git Attributes
# 
# cms-data.json is managed by the Admin Panel on the dedicated `cms-data` branch.
# VS Code / developers work on `main` and should NEVER accidentally overwrite Admin
# Panel data with a stale local copy of this file.
#
# Setting merge=ours means: if a merge/pull touches this file, Git keeps YOUR
# current version (the version already on the branch you're merging INTO) and
# ignores the incoming side. Combined with the `cms-data` branch architecture this
# means:
#   • On main: merges keep main's copy  → VS Code pushes are always safe
#   • On cms-data: merges keep cms-data's copy → Admin Panel data is always safe
#
# The real source of truth is always determined at RUNTIME by the /api/cms endpoint
# which compares lastSyncedAt timestamps from both branches and serves the newest.

src/data/cms-data.json merge=ours
